  "summary": "Peoria (AZ) police credited Flock ALPR cameras with locating a missing 82-year-old man with cognitive decline after his wife provided his license plate. The article notes a public-records audit showing 1,290 Flock searches in a month and public-comment pushback at a City Council meeting, though the chief said no discussions of canceling the contract are underway.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "A recent Flock network audit obtained by Arizona's Family through a public records request found that between July 14 and Aug. 14, Peoria police made 1,290 searches of the Flock system with 152 of those being for missing, endangered or runaway people.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "deploying a city-scaled surveillance system interconnected with neighboring jurisdictions through the same vendor without tactical comms, a road map. It's just an egregious breach of our trust honestly",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "Chief Intrieri said there have not been any conversations of canceling the Flock contract.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    }
  ],
